WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.666
- [Narrator] While
dinosaurs roamed the Earth

00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:06.840
and pterosaurs ruled the sky,

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.530
sea monsters called ichthyosaurs

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.740
dominated the world's oceans.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.570
Ichthyosaurs were ancient
reptilian predators.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.050
They first appeared

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.700
about 251 million years ago

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.720
during the Triassic Period.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.510
20 million years before
dinosaurs came about.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.380
True to their name,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.670
which means fish lizards in Greek,

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.020
the earliest ichthyosaurs

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.790
looked much like lizards with fins.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.920
Over the course of their
100 million year existence,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.520
their bodies transformed

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.970
and became more akin to fish in shape.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.140
They had long narrow skulls

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.990
and jaws that were lined with sharp teeth.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.140
These teeth were used to catch prey

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.480
like fish and squid.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.779
Their eyes were the largest

00:00:55.779 --> 00:00:58.270
ever recorded of any animal

00:00:58.270 --> 00:00:59.350
which helped them see

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.050
through the dark waters of the deep ocean.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.320
In fact one species had eyes

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.860
that were over 10 inches wide.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.680
Their bodies ranged in size.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.170
Some barely reached
the length of two feet.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.400
While the longest specimen

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.560
was about 85 feet long.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.280
They had paddle like fins

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.620
and a vertical tail

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.280
which help ichthyosaurs,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.030
despite their great size,

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.740
zip through water at speeds

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.720
of over 22 miles per hour.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.780
All together these qualities

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.170
put ichthyosaurs at the top

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.980
of the marine food chain.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.160
By the late Cretaceous Period,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.851
about 25 million years

00:01:39.851 --> 00:01:43.109
before an asteroid
wiped out the dinosaurs,

00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:45.590
ichthyosaurs became extinct.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.320
Some scientist believe

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.300
it may have been due

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.180
to severe climate change.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.880
But the exact reason why

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.127
these early sea monsters died out

00:01:55.127 --> 00:01:57.060
is still a mystery.

